  "question": {
    "text": "The tangent at any point on the curve <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> makes intercepts on the coordinate axes as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>16</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>32</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>64</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be a point on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> … <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Differentiating&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;w.r.t. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>, we get,&nbsp;<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />The slope of the tangent at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />So, the equation of the tangent is<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;(from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>)<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>intercept <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>intercept <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>"
  }
}